PREREQUISITES
   - This VALE Framework enablement kit was built with MVS 20.1, virtuoso 18.1
     ISR10, and Pegasus 19.12
   - Advanced Node GPDK v1.0

QUICK START:
1. Configure this directory with ./VALEconfig.csh 
   - First, setenv CDS_MVS_IMF_CM <to this directory containing IMFdefaults.il>
   - Second, setenv GPDK_INSTALL_DIR to the top level GPDK directory containing
     the "vale" directory
   - Third, run ./VALEconfig.csh in the "vale" directory
2. Ensure MVS is set correctly, and in the path:
   - setenv MVS <MVS 20.1>
   - setenv DFMHOME $MVSHOME
   - set path = ($path $MVSHOME/bin $MVSHOME/tools/bin)
3. Add load("<path to file>/cdsinitLoadVALE.il") to your .cdsinit, or
   - Use the testcases/.cdsinit
4. Start Virtuoso


Contents of the GPDK vale directory:

VALEconfig.csh

   Run this script in the "vale" directory to auto-update the paths in
   IMFdefaults.il

cdsinitLoadVALE.il

   Virtuoso setup script to enable VALE.  Requires Cadence MVS 19.2
   (MVS 20.1 is recommended)
   VALE requires Component Modules. Set the CDS_MVS_IMF_CM env var to point
   to the Component Module directory.  Or, use GPDK_INSTALL_DIR.  

IMFdefaults.il

   VALE Configuration File

Include:

   VALE Component Module Include Directory: contains support files for various
   example Component Modules in the GPDK.

SKILL:
   VALE Framework top-level Component Module definitions
cxt/
   64bit/
      VALE Framework Helper functions
docs/
   VALE Framework Component Modules Descriptions (documentation)

docs:

   Documentation README 
